      <h2>How the texts came to be</h2>
      <p>Sacred texts reach their community in different ways — this affects the <b>authority</b> believers give them:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Directly revealed:</b> the <b>Qur'an</b> is held to be God's exact words revealed to Muhammad. Shruti texts in Hinduism are held to be eternal truth "heard" by sages.</li>
        <li><b>Written under inspiration:</b> many Christians see the <b>Bible</b> as written by human authors inspired by God.</li>
        <li><b>Compiled from oral tradition:</b> the <b>Tipitaka</b> and the <b>Vedas</b> were memorised and recited for generations before being written; the <b>Talmud</b> records the rabbis' oral discussion.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><b>Oral vs written:</b> a text can be authoritative long before it is written down. Careful memorisation and recitation preserved many scriptures for centuries.</p>
    </section>

